[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Windows-managed host memory for Spice campaigns

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RUN-HOST-MEMORY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Defer host memory allocation to Windows
STATEMENT: >>>
Ordinary Spice builds, simulations, tests and property/fuzz batches on this Windows host shall not enforce process-tree or aggregate host RAM caps, free-RAM admission thresholds or memory-triggered process termination. Windows shall manage host memory. Mutation testing is the sole exception: observe mutant process-tree memory and, when observed growth is out of control, apply a documented targeted limit or stop the positively identified runaway mutant tree. Record the observed growth, affected identity, intervention and incomplete outcomes; do not apply the exception as a whole-campaign cap or automatically classify resource-terminated mutants as test kills. Existing time budgets, cancellation, worker concurrency bounds, exclusive campaign lock, disk-space checks and E: output routing shall remain in force. Genuine allocation failures or OS terminations shall remain failed/incomplete evidence, not passing coverage. Parser/model/request-size validation shall not be disabled by this host policy.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Explicit user instruction, November 15, 2026. Configuration trace: project AGENTS.md and spice-nightly-endurance-campaign automation. Source inspection: Run-VerifiedSoak.ps1, Run-Endurance.ps1, Endurance.cs and FrameworkMutations.cs do not enforce the historical external host memory guards. Old raw artifact scripts and failed evidence remain historical, unmodified data. No new runtime or coverage claim follows from this policy change.
<<<
